---
import ExperimentControls from './ExperimentControls.astro';
import PhysicsDataPanel from './PhysicsDataPanel.astro';
---
<div class="playground-shell" data-playground>
  <div class="experiment-browser">
    <label for="experiment-category">Atlas</label>
    <select id="experiment-category" aria-label="Experiment category"></select>
    <div class="experiment-tabs" role="tablist" aria-label="Physics experiments"></div>
  </div>
  <div class="experiment-layout">
    <ExperimentControls />
    <section id="experiment-stage" class="experiment-stage" role="tabpanel" aria-labelledby="tab-projectile" tabindex="0">
      <div class="canvas-frame">
        <canvas id="physics-canvas" aria-label="Interactive physics experiment"></canvas>
        <div class="canvas-badge"><span id="experiment-number">EXPERIMENT 01</span><strong id="experiment-name">Projectile target</strong></div>
      </div>
      <div id="experiment-actions" class="experiment-actions" aria-label="Experiment actions"></div>
      <p id="keyboard-help" class="keyboard-help">Keyboard: Space launch/pause · R reset · N new target · Arrow keys aim</p>
    </section>
    <PhysicsDataPanel />
  </div>
  <section id="experiment-details" class="experiment-details" aria-label="Formula and physical explanation"></section>
  <noscript>
    <section class="no-script-note">
      <h2>Physics Playground needs JavaScript for the live instruments.</h2>
      <p>The projectile experiment uses <code>x(t)=v₀cos(θ)t</code> and <code>y(t)=v₀sin(θ)t−½gt²</code>. The double pendulum integrates coupled nonlinear equations with RK4. Wave Lab visualizes superposed damped waves. The Electromagnetism Atlas evaluates <code>E=(1/4πε₀)Σqᵢ(r−rᵢ)/|r−rᵢ|³</code> while excluding point-charge singularities.</p>
    </section>
  </noscript>
</div>
